# Stack & Versions

## Core Framework

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Next.js | 15.5.8 | App Router, Turbopack for builds |
| React | 19.1.2 | Concurrent features, `use` hook available |
| TypeScript | 5.9.2 | Strict mode enabled |
| pnpm | 9.15.4 | Required package manager |

### Next.js 15 Best Practices

- Use `async` Server Components for data fetching; avoid `getServerSideProps`/`getStaticProps`
- Prefer Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only when using hooks/browser APIs
- Use `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` for Suspense boundaries
- Route handlers go in `app/api/` with `route.ts` files
- Dynamic routes use `[param]` folder naming
- Build uses Turbopack (`next build --turbopack`)

### React 19 Best Practices

- Use the `use` hook for reading promises/context in render
- `ref` is now a regular prop—no need for `forwardRef` in most cases
- Actions: `useActionState`, `useFormStatus`, `useOptimistic` for forms
- Avoid legacy patterns (`defaultProps`, string refs)

## UI & Styling

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Chakra UI | 3.26.0 | v3 with Ark UI primitives |
| Emotion | 11.14.0 | CSS-in-JS for Chakra |
| Motion | 12.23.22 | Animation library (formerly Framer Motion) |
| react-icons | 5.5.0 | Icon library |
| recharts | 3.2.1 | Chart components |

### Chakra UI v3 Best Practices

- v3 uses Ark UI primitives under the hood—API differs from v2
- Import from `@chakra-ui/react` (not sub-packages)
- Use semantic tokens from theme config (`components/theme/config.tsx`)
- Prefer composition: `<Box>`, `<Flex>`, `<Stack>`, `<Grid>`
- Use `asChild` prop to merge styling onto child elements
- Color mode via `next-themes` integration

### Motion Best Practices

- Import `motion` components from `motion` package
- Use CSS spring easing for natural animations (MCP tool available)
- Prefer `whileHover`, `whileTap` for micro-interactions
- Use `layout` prop for shared layout animations
- Keep animations under 400ms for responsiveness

## State & Data

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| TanStack Query | 5.85.6 | Server state management |
| Zustand | 5.0.8 | Client state management |
| Zod | 4.1.5 | Schema validation |

### TanStack Query v5 Best Practices

- Queries return `{ data, isPending, isError }` (not `isLoading`)
- Use `queryOptions()` helper for type-safe query definitions
- Mutations: use `useMutation` with `onSuccess`/`onError`
- Prefetch in Server Components with `prefetchQuery`
- Configure staleTime/gcTime per query type
- Devtools available via `@tanstack/react-query-devtools`

### Zustand v5 Best Practices

- Use `create` with `persist` middleware for localStorage
- Selectors: `useStore((s) => s.value)` to avoid re-renders
- No providers needed—stores are global
- Avoid storing derived state; compute in selectors
- Settings store: `lib/stores/settings.ts`

### Zod v4 Best Practices

- v4 has improved performance and tree-shaking
- Use `z.object()` for API response schemas
- Prefer `z.infer<typeof schema>` for TypeScript types
- Use `.transform()` for data normalization
- Schemas live in `lib/schemas/` and `services/**/schemas.ts`

## Internationalization

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| i18next | 25.4.2 | Core i18n library |
| react-i18next | 15.7.3 | React bindings |
| next-i18n-router | 5.5.3 | Locale routing |

### i18n Best Practices

- Translations in `i18n/languages/*.json`
- Use `useTranslation` hook in Client Components
- Server Components: use `i18n/server.ts` utilities
- Locale detected via middleware (`middleware.ts`)
- Always add new keys to `en.json` first

## Blockchain SDKs

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| @vechain/sdk-core | 2.0.7 | VeChain core utilities |
| @vechain/sdk-network | 2.0.7 | Thor node client |
| viem | 2.36.0 | EVM utilities (ABI, encoding) |
| bignumber.js | 9.3.1 | Arbitrary precision math |

### VeChain SDK Best Practices

- Use services in `services/thor/` for node interactions
- Network switching handled by settings store
- Always validate responses with Zod schemas
- Use `bignumber.js` for token amounts (avoid floating point)

### viem Best Practices

- Use for ABI encoding/decoding, address validation
- Prefer viem utilities over manual hex manipulation
- Type-safe contract interactions with `getContract`

